    slug: "server-side-analytics-privacy-first",
    desc: "Why client-side tracking is broken and how we use server-side GTM to bypass ad-blockers and protect user privacy.",
    content:
      "Third-party cookies are dying, and ad-blockers are more prevalent than ever. If you are relying on client-side Google Analytics snippets, you are likely losing 30% of your data to browser restrictions. At Maldonite, we’ve shifted to Server-Side GTM (Google Tag Manager) and first-party data collection. Instead of sending data directly from the user's browser to an analytics provider, we send it to our own secure server first. This allows us to scrub sensitive user information, anonymize IP addresses, and ensure compliance with GDPR and CCPA before the data ever leaves our environment. This isn't just about privacy; it's about performance. By moving tracking scripts off the client’s browser, we significantly reduce the 'JavaScript weight' of the site, leading to faster load times and better Core Web Vitals. Server-side tracking also allows us to enrich data in real-time. If a user makes a purchase, our server can verify the transaction in our database and send the 'True Revenue' to Facebook or Google Ads, preventing the common issue of duplicate or fake conversions. We also implement 'Custom Proxies' for our tracking endpoints, making them invisible to standard ad-blockers. This ensures that our clients have 100% accurate data to base their business decisions on. In a world where data privacy is becoming a legal battleground, Maldonite’s approach provides a 'Safe Harbor' for your analytics. We help you build a relationship with your users based on trust and transparency, while still getting the insights you need to grow your bottom line. It’s a win-win for both the business and the consumer. If you aren't tracking on the server, you are flying blind. We make sure your data is clean, compliant, and complete.",
